<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carol II of Romania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carol II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> from 1930 to 1940. Having renounced his rights to the throne in 1925, he returned in 1930 to displace his young son Michael, and in 1938 he abolished the political parties and set up a royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a>. After Romania lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukovina">Bukovina</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-dobruja">Southern Dobruja</a> in 1940, he was forced to abdicate in favour of Michael and went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carol-ii-of-romania.jpg" alt="Carol II of Romania" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carol_II_of_Romania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Such regimes often suppressed fascist movements: Austrian Nazis assassinated Dollfuss, and King <b>Carol II of Romania</b> ordered the execution of the Iron Guard leader Corneliu Zelea Codreanu.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/conservatism">Conservatism · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>Land reform and the 1923 constitution followed, but the interwar years saw the fascist Iron Guard and <b>Carol II</b>'s royal dictatorship from 1938.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Kingdom of Romania</a></li></ul></section>
